		(property "Usage" "Upper leg of the ILIM_HIZ divider from REGN; sets the hardware backstop input-current clamp at exactly 2.00A (V_ILIM_HIZ = 1V + 800mOhm x IINDPM = 2.6V, using REGN=4.8V typ and R302/R303=110k/130k). This is a resistor-set analog ceiling the charger enforces regardless of the IINDPM register value -- independent of firmware/I2C misconfiguration. Chosen to size VBUS/VUSB/VDC input-path copper for 2A instead of the IC 5A max."
			(at 99.06 210.82 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Placement" "Not switching-noise-sensitive; place near the ILIM_HIZ pin for routing convenience."
			(at 99.06 210.82 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
