		(property "Note" "Footprint filename says BQ25792 -- EasyEDA export-tool naming artifact for the sibling part. This IS the correct QFN-29 4x4mm 0.4mm-pitch package for BQ25798RQMR."
			(at 262.89 298.45 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Firmware Constraint" "PCB copper for PMID/SYS/SW1/SW2/BAT (Power_2A net class) is sized for 2A, not the IC's 5A max. R302/R303 hardware-clamp INPUT current (IINDPM) to 2.00A via ILIM_HIZ, independent of firmware. There is NO equivalent hardware clamp on ICHG (charge current) -- it is a pure I2C register (REG03, 50mA-5000mA, resets to PROG-resistor default of 1A on POR/watchdog/REG_RST). Firmware MUST NOT set ICHG above 2000mA (2A); doing so can drive charge-side copper beyond its rated current, since in buck mode (VBUS greater than VBAT) charge current can exceed input current."
			(at 262.89 300.99 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "MPN" "BQ25798RQMR"
